            {
              "id": "895b03f3-261a-4157-9627-84d9ee984fd0",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Ender's Game &amp; Philosophy: The Logic Gate is Down</strong></em> is a collection of essays edited by Kevin S. Decker, published by Wiley, July 22, 2013."
            },
            {
              "id": "4fe0d7b3-2020-4c10-b1dd-df844f2a2568",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "7fa4ee7b-ff67-4f6d-a34d-932e5af6d9b3",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>A threat to humanity portending the end of our species lurks in the cold recesses of space. Our only hope is an eleven-year-old boy. Celebrating the long-awaited release of the movie adaptation of Orson Scott Card’s novel about highly trained child geniuses fighting a race of invading aliens, this collection of original essays probes key philosophical questions raised in the narrative, including the ethics of child soldiers, politics on the internet, and the morality of war and genocide.</em>"
            }
          ]
        },
